WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Artifacts are signals or distortions not generated by cardiac electrical activity. They can mimic dangerous rhythms or obscure real ones. Begin with the patient, then compare the tracing with pulse and perfusion, other leads and any visible source of movement.
伪差是并非来自心脏电活动的信号或失真，可模拟危险节律，也可掩盖真正节律。应从患者开始，再比较波形与脉搏、灌注、其他导联及可见运动来源。

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:36.552
An alert patient with an effective pulse does not have sustained VF merely because one lead is chaotic. Conversely, artifact can coexist with genuine arrest. If circulation is absent, initiate the appropriate response while checking equipment without prolonged interruptions.
清醒且有有效脉搏的患者，不会仅因一个导联杂乱就被认定持续室颤。反过来，伪差也可与真正骤停并存；循环不存在时，应一边按流程响应，一边核对设备，不能长时间中断处置。

00:00:36.552 --> 00:00:56.808
Motion artifact often produces large, erratic deflections around patient movement, procedures or transport. Muscle tremor can produce fine rapid oscillation, for example with shivering or Parkinsonian movement. Either can imitate rhythm abnormalities, so appearance alone is not enough.
运动伪差常在患者移动、操作或转运时出现较大、无规则偏转；肌颤可产生细快振荡，如寒战或帕金森样运动。二者均可能模拟节律异常，不能仅凭外观判断。

00:00:56.808 --> 00:01:16.920
Look for underlying QRS complexes that maintain their timing and compare another lead with the patient’s pulse. Support painful limbs, warm a cold patient and offer reassurance. Improvement after these actions supports an artifact explanation but does not erase a coexisting clinical problem.
应寻找仍按原时序出现的底层 QRS，并把其他导联与脉搏比较。可支持疼痛肢体、为寒冷患者保暖并安抚。随后信号改善支持伪差解释，但不能消除并存临床问题。

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:35.880
Baseline wander is slow movement of the reference line, commonly associated with breathing or poor contact. A loose electrode can create intermittent signal loss or a flat segment. Neither pattern proves a true atrial rhythm or asystole until patient and equipment have been assessed.
基线漂移是参考线缓慢移动，常与呼吸或接触不良相关；松动电极可造成间歇信号丢失或平段。在评估患者及设备之前，这些形态都不能证明真正心房节律或心静止。

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:55.584
Check the electrode site, adhesive, cable and connection. Dry sweat and remove interfering hair using appropriate equipment. Use the manufacturer-approved skin preparation and allow the site to dry before applying a fresh electrode. Record the correction and whether the repeat tracing improved.
应检查电极位置、粘附、线缆与连接，擦干汗液并用合适工具去除妨碍接触的毛发。按厂商认可方法准备皮肤，干燥后贴新电极，并记录纠正措施与复测改善情况。

00:01:55.584 --> 00:02:16.680
In this setting, mains-related sixty-hertz interference may create a dense fuzzy baseline. Inspect nearby power cords, chargers and equipment, and keep signal cables away from likely interference sources. Do not assume every fuzzy baseline is VF or every flat-looking segment is true asystole.
在本地环境，60赫兹电源相关干扰可使基线密集发毛。应检查附近电线、充电器与设备，使信号线远离可能干扰源。不能把所有毛糙基线当室颤，也不能把所有平段当真正心静止。

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:36.312
Use safe equipment arrangements and device instructions; do not disconnect essential monitoring or treatment simply to improve a tracing. If a change in equipment position or power arrangement is appropriate, reassess signal quality and document the result. Persistent uncertainty belongs in the handover.
应遵循安全设备布置和说明，不能仅为了改善波形就断开必要监护或治疗。若适合调整设备位置或供电方式，应复核信号并记录结果；持续不确定性须交接说明。

00:02:36.312 --> 00:02:54.672
The school contrasts tremor with VF, baseline wander with flutter and movement with tachyarrhythmia. These are comparison exercises, not absolute rules. True tachyarrhythmias can be irregular; artifact can affect several leads; illness and movement can occur together.
学校对比肌颤与室颤、基线漂移与房扑、运动与快速心律失常。这些是比较练习，不是绝对规则：真正快速心律失常也可不齐，伪差也可影响多个导联，疾病与运动也可能同时出现。

00:02:54.672 --> 00:03:12.864
Combine clinical pulse status, repeated acquisition, lead consistency and whether underlying complexes remain visible. A poor signal limits confidence. If you cannot distinguish the rhythm reliably, state that clearly and obtain appropriate assistance while continuing care.
应合并临床脉搏状态、重复采集、导联一致性及底层波群是否可见。信号差会限制把握度；若无法可靠区分节律，应明确说明并取得适当支持，同时继续照护。

00:03:12.864 --> 00:03:34.320
Preparation includes dignity, anatomical landmarks and secure contact, not just pressing the acquisition button. Position the patient as clinically appropriate and obtain a stationary recording when feasible. For suspected ACS, efficient preparation helps achieve the school’s timely diagnostic acquisition target.
准备不仅是按采集键，还包括尊严、解剖标志及可靠接触。应按病情安排体位，在可行时静止采集；疑似 ACS 时，高效准备有助于达到学校及时取得诊断记录的目标。

00:03:34.320 --> 00:03:52.128
If the first tracing remains unreliable, repeat after a targeted correction rather than changing many variables without recording what happened. Preserve clinically important earlier tracings and their times so the receiving team can distinguish technical change from genuine evolution.
若首份记录仍不可靠，应有针对性地纠正后复测，不能同时改动许多因素却不记录。应保留有临床意义的既往记录及时间，让接收团队区分技术改变和真正病情演变。

00:03:52.128 --> 00:04:10.008
Document the artifact, why it prevented reliable interpretation, the corrective action and the outcome of the repeat. Include symptoms and perfusion at the same time. Saying only that the second ECG was normal hides the reason the earlier tracing looked different.
应记录伪差类型、为何妨碍可靠判读、纠正措施及复测结果，同时记录症状和灌注。只说“第二份正常”会隐去前一份为何不同的原因。

00:04:10.008 --> 00:04:28.248
A complete handover might say that movement obscured atrial activity, contact and positioning were corrected, and a repeat showed a describable rhythm while symptoms persisted. The repeat improves electrical evidence but does not, by itself, resolve the patient’s complaint.
完整交接可说明：运动遮蔽心房活动，已纠正接触与体位，复测出现可描述节律，但症状仍持续。复测改善了电学证据，却不能单独解决患者主诉。
